url: "https://github.com/spectralbranding/philosophy-papers"
abstract: >
  Public mirror for a line of philosophy-of-science work asking when a claim about
  where a system ends has empirical content, and what a domain must supply for such
  a claim to be testable at all. Each paper directory carries the paper, its
  proposition and dependency graph, its ontology module, its analysis code, and a
  manifest naming the canonical home of every data artifact it depends on. Cite the
  individual paper rather than this repository; per-paper CITATION.cff files and
  concept DOIs are in each directory.
keywords:
  - "philosophy of science"
  - "system boundaries"
  - "scientific realism"
  - "underdetermination"
  - "philosophy of measurement"
  - "individuation"
